---
import {url, base} from '../lib/base';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';import {records} from '../lib/catalogue';import manifest from '../../qa/import-manifest.json';const articles=await records('articles');
---
<Site title="Evidence & research" active="Research"><div class="container page"><div class="page-heading"><h1>Clarity starts with evidence.</h1><p>The aim is to translate technical research into useful questions, while keeping uncertainty visible.</p></div><div class="data-note"><a href={url('/intelligence/')}><strong>AI &amp; semiconductor intelligence →</strong></a> Explore 12 source-linked briefs, technologies, companies and research catalysts.</div><div class="research-grid"><section><span class="eyebrow">01 / What you are reading</span><h2>Imported research.</h2><p>This edition imports technology and company notes from Future Trends. Original claims, source counts, estimates and financial observations are preserved; they have not been independently fact-checked during the migration. Records marked <em>Editorial brief</em> were compiled from named public sources in November 2026 and are labelled separately on each page.</p><p>Source commit: <code>{manifest.sourceCommit.slice(0,12)}</code>. Local import: 16 November 2026.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">02 / Two equal lenses</span><h2>Commercial meaning.</h2><p>Business readers ask what changes in capability, cost or workflow. Investors ask who could capture value, what must be funded and what would invalidate the thesis. Neither lens turns a technology milestone into a guaranteed financial return.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">03 / Numbers need context</span><h2>Labels are not probabilities.</h2><p>Source confidence scores, timing signals and source counts are model or editorial metadata. They are not verified probabilities of technical success or investment return. Imported BUY/SELL signals appear only in the timestamped source snapshot.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">04 / Shared and traceable</span><h2>One record, many views.</h2><p>Technology records use stable IDs. Website pages and evergreen slides reference those same records. Source Markdown is retained for provenance; exported snapshots can preserve the historical version of a briefing.</p></section></div><h2 class="subheading">Original research & reference pages</h2><div class="article-links">{articles.map(a=><a href={url(`/read/${a.id}/`)}>{a.title}<span>{a.sourcePath}</span></a>)}</div></div></Site>
